man services resources through 211 Orange County", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "high", "notes": "The online Family Service Request Form is closed ('we are no longer accepting requests through this form'), although the FSC home page and the County pocket guide still point to it. Family Access Points by region are listed at https://familysolutionscollaborative.org/access-points/. The County says the family bed reservation system refers to 65 emergency shelter and 13 transitional housing family units as openings occur."}, {"id": "yale-navigation-center", "name": "Yale Navigation Center", "organization": "PATH (People Assisting the Homeless), under contract with the County of Orange", "category": "shelter", "tags": ["emergency-shelter", "navigation-center", "central-spa", "couples", "referral-only", "bed-reservation"], "description": "County emergency shelter in Santa Ana for up to 425 adult individuals and couples experiencing homelessness in the Central Service Planning Area, with supportive services focused on stabilization and permanent housing.", "services": ["Emergency shelter", "Supportive services", "Permanent housing placement support"], "eligibility": "Adult individuals and couples experiencing homelessness in the Central Service Planning Area. Entry by referral only: approved Central SPA referring partners, or a Central SPA Access Point reached by calling 2-1-1.", "population": ["adults", "couples"], "how_to_access": "referral-only", "referral_required": true, "phone": "(800) 364-2221", "address": "2229 S. Yale St., Santa Ana, CA 92704", "city": "Santa Ana", "hours": null, "languages": null, "cost": null, "website": "https://epath.org/regions/orange-county/", "source_url": "https://ceo.oc.gov/care-coordination/homeless-services/shelter-programs", "source_quote": "PATH provides shelter and supportive services for up to 425 adult individuals and couples experiencing homelessness in the Central Service Planning Area (SPA).", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "high", "notes": "The phone is the OC Outreach & Engagement referral hotline given on the County page, not a front desk. Do not send anyone to the address without a referral. The County's Central SPA pocket guide (https://ceo.oc.gov/sites/ceo/files/2025-10/Pocket%20Guide%20Resource%20Directory%20-%20Central%20Updated%207.28.2025.pdf, dated 2025) lists a different referral number, 714-785-9889. Central SPA: Costa Mesa, Fountain Valley, Garden Grove, Huntington Beach, Midway City, Newport Beach, Santa Ana, Seal Beach, Tustin, Westminster."}, {"id": "bridges-at-kraemer-place", "name": "Bridges at Kraemer Place", "organization": "PATH (People Assisting the Homeless), under contract with the County of Orange", "category": "shelter", "tags": ["emergency-shelter", "north-spa", "referral-only", "bed-reservation"], "description": "County emergency shelter in Anaheim for up to 200 adult individuals experiencing homelessness in the North Service Planning Area, with supportive services focused on stabilization and permanent housing.", "services": ["Emergency shelter", "Supportive services", "Permanent housing placement support"], "eligibility": "Adult individuals experiencing homelessness in the North Service Planning Area. Entry by referral only: approved North SPA referring partners, or a North SPA Access Point reached by calling 2-1-1.", "population": ["adults"], "how_to_access": "referral-only", "referral_required": true, "phone": "(800) 364-2221", "address": "1000 N. Kraemer Place, Anaheim, CA 92806", "city": "Anaheim", "hours": null, "languages": null, "cost": null, "website": "https://epath.org/regions/orange-county/", "source_url": "https://ceo.oc.gov/care-coordination/homeless-services/shelter-programs", "source_quote": "Bridges provides shelter and supportive services for up to 200 adult individuals experiencing homelessness in the North Service Planning Area (SPA).", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "high", "notes": "Operator changed in 2026: PATH states it became operator on July 1, 2026, but 211OC's record (last verified 2026-02-17) still lists Mercy House Living Centers with an unrelated agency address. The phone is the OC Outreach & Engagement referral hotline, not a front desk. Do not send anyone to the address without a referral. North SPA: Anaheim, Brea, Buena Park, Cypress, Fullerton, La Habra, La Palma, Los Alamitos, Orange, Placentia, Rossmoor, Stanton, Villa Park, Yorba Linda."}, {"id": "costa-mesa-bridge-shelter", "name": "Costa Mesa Bridge Shelter", "organization": "City of Costa Mesa Network for Homeless Solutions (operated by Mercy House)", "category": "shelter", "tags": ["emergency-shelter", "bridge-shelter", "city-ties", "referral-only", "costa-mesa", "newport-beach"], "description": "70-bed city shelter providing interim housing with wrap-around services toward permanent housing. Guests are admitted by referral only, through the City's 24-hour Network for Homeless Solutions hotline.", "services": ["Interim housing", "Help locating and securing permanent housing", "Help with barriers to housing and employment", "Meals prepared on site", "Transportation to and from the shelter"], "eligibility": "Admission by referral only. The City gives direct assistance to people with Costa Mesa ties: a household member who has lived or worked in Costa Mesa for the preceding 36 months, or who attends school in the city.", "population": ["adults"], "how_to_access": "referral-only", "referral_required": true, "phone": "(714) 754-5346", "address": null, "city": "Costa Mesa", "hours": "24-hour NHS Hotline", "languages": null, "cost": null, "website": "https://www.costamesaca.gov/government/departments-and-divisions/city-manager-s-office/network-for-homeless-solutions", "source_url": "https://www.costamesaca.gov/government/departments-and-divisions/city-manager-s-office/network-for-homeless-solutions/costa-mesa-bridge-shelter/contact-shelter", "source_quote": "Guests are admitted into the Bridge Shelter by referral only.", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "high", "notes": "Bed count conflict: the City page says 70 beds, 211OC's record says 100. Newport Beach says it partners with Costa Mesa for shelter beds here. The shelter's street address was not on the pages fetched. costamesaca.gov returns HTTP 403 to plain scripted requests; it loaded only with browser-like headers."}, {"id": "huntington-beach-navigation-center", "name": "Huntington Beach Navigation Center", "organization": "City of Huntington Beach (operated by Mercy House)", "category": "shelter", "tags": ["emergency-shelter", "navigation-center", "city-ties", "referral-only", "couples", "huntington-beach"], "description": "City navigation center that can shelter up to 164 adults and couples with ties to Huntington Beach. No walk-ups: people must be prescreened and referred by the City's social workers or Homeless Task Force officers.", "services": ["Emergency shelter", "Case management", "Access to services on the path to housing"], "eligibility": "Experiencing homelessness in Huntington Beach, not sheltered elsewhere, with significant and verifiable ties to the city (for example a permanent address there within the last five years, current or recent employment there, full-time enrollment at Golden West College, or a close family member living there). No open felony warrant; registered sex or arson offenders are not admitted; must be able to meet all Activities of Daily Living.", "population": ["adults", "couples"], "how_to_access": "referral-only", "referral_required": true, "phone": "(714) 536-5576", "address": "17642 Beach Boulevard", "city": "Huntington Beach", "hours": "City social worker walk-in office hours: Huntington Beach Police Department front lobby, 2000 Main Street, Tuesday 9:00 a.m. – 11:00 a.m. and Wednesday 10:00 a.m. – 12:00 p.m.", "languages": null, "cost": null, "website": "https://huntingtonbeachca.gov/departments/city_manager/homeless_solutions/index.php", "source_url": "https://huntingtonbeachca.gov/departments/city_manager/homeless_solutions/hb_navigation_center.php", "source_quote": "The Center can shelter up to 164 adults and couples with ties to Huntington Beach.", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "high", "notes": "Phone and office hours are from the City's Homeless Assistance page (https://huntingtonbeachca.gov/departments/city_manager/homeless_solutions/homeless_assistance.php), which also lists office hours at Community United Methodist Church, 6652 Heil Avenue (Wednesday 1:30 p.m. - 3:00 p.m.) and Refuge Calvary Chapel, 7800 Edinger Avenue (Thursday 11:00 a.m. to 12:30 p.m.). The page says people who do not meet the requirements can still be connected to other services. Do not send anyone to the shelter address without a referral."}, {"id": "buena-park-navigation-center", "name": "Buena Park Navigation Center", "organization": "City of Buena Park (operated by Mercy House)", "category": "shelter", "tags": ["emergency-shelter", "navigation-center", "north-spa", "referral-only", "buena-park"], "description": "150-bed temporary shelter for North Orange County (North SPA) cities, with host cities such as Buena Park given priority. Clients are received on a referral basis only; walk-ins are not permitted.", "services": ["Temporary shelter", "Healthcare and other on-site services"], "eligibility": "Beds are designated for North SPA cities only, with host cities (including Buena Park) having priority. Referrals are typically made by police homeless liaison officers, the Homeless Outreach Team and the County of Orange.", "population": ["adults"], "how_to_access": "referral-only", "referral_required": true, "phone": "(714) 235-3296", "address": "6494 Caballero Blvd., Buena Park, CA 90620", "city": "Buena Park", "hours": null, "languages": null, "cost": null, "website": "https://www.buenapark.com/residents/navigation_center.php", "source_url": "https://www.buenapark.com/residents/navigation_center.php", "source_quote": "The center will only receive clients on a referral-basis; walk-ins are not permitted.", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "high", "notes": "The same page lists the Buena Park Homeless Outreach Team at (714) 236-3877. The City page does not state an age rule; 'adults' follows 211OC's record ('18 years and older', last verified 2026-02-17), which also lists a different contact number, (714) 410-4060 ext. 281. Do not send anyone to the address without a referral."}, {"id": "central-cities-navigation-center", "name": "Central Cities Navigation Center (CCNC)", "organization": "City of Garden Grove with Fountain Valley and Westminster (operated by Volunteers of America of Los Angeles)", "category": "shelter", "tags": ["emergency-shelter", "navigation-center", "central-spa", "referral-only", "garden-grove", "fountain-valley", "westminster", "pets"], "description": "Year-round, low-barrier navigation center in Garden Grove with 85 beds, offering transitional emergency housing and wrap-around services to homeless adults referred from Garden Grove, Fountain Valley and Westminster. No walk-ins.", "services": ["Emergency housing (length of stay up to 120 days)", "1-on-1 case management", "Mental health and substance use counseling resources", "Outpatient health services", "Employment assistance and job training", "Shuttle transportation", "Service animal and pet accommodation"], "eligibility": "18+, no children. No walk-in. Referral guidelines on the City page: by designated PD division (GGPD SRT, FVPD HLO, W HLO), the cities' contracted street outreach service providers, or through the bed reservation systems. Beds are split among Garden Grove (50), Fountain Valley (13) and Westminster (22).", "population": ["adults", "couples"], "how_to_access": "referral-only", "referral_required": true, "phone": null, "address": "13871 West Street, Garden Grove, CA 92843", "city": "Garden Grove", "hours": "24/7 including city holidays", "languages": null, "cost": null, "website": "https://ggcity.org/navigation-center", "source_url": "https://ggcity.org/navigation-center", "source_quote": "offering low-barrier transitional emergency housing and wrap-around services to homeless individuals in Orange County's Central Service Planning Area", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "high", "notes": "No public phone number: the City page lists none and 211OC's record says 'See chart for referral information'. The City page still says Garden Grove 'is developing' the center even though it reports an opening date of June 5, 2024. Do not send anyone to the address without a referral."}, {"id": "wiseplace", "name": "WISEPlace: shelter and housing help for unaccompanied women", "organization": "WISEPlace", "category": "shelter", "tags": ["women", "emergency-shelter", "case-management", "financial-assistance", "survivors"], "description": "Temporary shelter for unaccompanied individuals experiencing homelessness, with 1:1 case management, counseling, employment support and housing search help. Also offers financial assistance, such as a deposit or temporary rental assistance, to eligible people who are homeless but not seeking shelter.", "services": ["Temporary shelter", "1:1 case management and counseling", "Employment support", "Housing search assistance", "Help with job, housing and public benefits applications", "Financial assistance (deposit, temporary rental assistance, utility deposit)"], "eligibility": "Unaccompanied women / individuals experiencing homelessness. Request help by phone or the online inquiry form. Financial assistance has separate eligibility; the form asks about ties to the City of Santa Ana.", "population": ["women", "adults without children"], "how_to_access": "mixed", "referral_required": false, "phone": "(714)542-3577", "address": null, "city": "Santa Ana", "hours": null, "languages": null, "cost": null, "website": "https://wiseplace.org/", "source_url": "https://wiseplace.org/get-help/", "source_quote": "WISEPlace offers unaccompanied individuals experiencing homelessness a safe place by providing temporary shelter.", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "high", "notes": "Street address deliberately omitted: 211OC lists WISEPlace as a Coordinated Entry access point for survivors, and this seed gives a phone line only for survivor-serving programs. The site footer says its focus is 'unaccompanied women' while the help page says 'unaccompanied individuals', so confirm who is eligible when calling."}, {"id": "oc-outreach-and-engagement", "name": "OC Outreach & Engagement (OC O&E)", "organization": "County of Orange (OC Health Care Agency / Office of Care Coordination)", "category": "housing-navigation", "tags": ["street-outreach", "unsheltered", "shelter-referral", "linkage", "behavioral-health"], "description": "County outreach teams serving people experiencing unsheltered homelessness, linking them to housing, physical health, behavioral health and other supportive services. The same hotline is the referral line the County lists for its two shelters.", "services": ["Street outreach", "Linkage to housing and shelter", "Linkage to physical and behavioral health care", "Referral line for Yale Navigation Center and Bridges at Kraemer Place"], "eligibility": "Individuals experiencing unsheltered homelessness in Orange County.", "population": ["adults"], "how_to_access": "phone", "referral_required": false, "phone": "800-364-2221", "address": null, "city": null, "hours": "MON – FRI 8 AM – 5 PM", "languages": null, "cost": null, "website": "https://ceo.oc.gov/office-care-coordination/get-help", "source_url": "https://ochealthinfo.com/services-programs/mental-health-crisis-recovery/adult-18-services/outreach-and-engagement", "source_quote": "The Orange County Outreach & Engagement (OC O&E) program serves individuals experiencing unsheltered homelessness in Orange County.", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "high", "notes": "Hours are from the County's Central SPA pocket guide (https://ceo.oc.gov/sites/ceo/files/2025-10/Pocket%20Guide%20Resource%20Directory%20-%20Central%20Updated%207.28.2025.pdf, dated 2025); the program page itself states no hours, so confirm. The County Get Help page says to call 9-1-1 for a medical emergency and the Crisis Assessment Team at (855) 625-4657 for a non-emergency mental health crisis."}, {"id": "hub-resource-center-orange", "name": "The HUB Resource Center (HRC)", "organization": "The HUB OC, in partnership with the City of Orange", "category": "hygiene-mail-storage", "tags": ["showers", "laundry", "mail", "meals", "clothing", "charging", "case-management", "coordinated-entry-access-point", "orange"], "description": "Drop-in resource center in the City of Orange for unhoused people: meals, showers, laundry, clothing, mail service and phone charging, plus a Housing 101 class and one-on-one casework. Services are first-come, first-served with same-day appointments.", "services": ["Meals & food access", "Showers", "Laundry services", "Clothing distribution", "Mail services", "Charging stations", "Transportation support", "Medical & health services", "Pet supplies", "Hygiene kits", "Case management and housing pathways (Housing 101 class, Open Casework)"], "eligibility": "Serves the unhoused population in partnership with the City of Orange. The site offers a separate resource list 'for those not living in Orange, CA'.", "population": ["adults"], "how_to_access": "walk-in", "referral_required": false, "phone": "(657) 767-5751", "address": "517 W. Struck Ave, Orange, CA 92867", "city": "Orange", "hours": "Monday, Tuesday, Thursday, Friday: Basic Needs 7am to 11am, Programming 11am to 3pm. Saturday: Basic Needs only, 9am to 1pm.", "languages": null, "cost": null, "website": "https://thehubresourcecenter.org/", "source_url": "https://thehubresourcecenter.org/services", "source_quote": "At the HRC our services operate on a fair and straightforward first-come, first-served basis, with same-day appointments ensuring timely assistance to those in need.", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "high", "notes": "Address and phone are from the site's home page. 211OC lists this site as a Coordinated Entry Access Point for individuals and veterans in the North SPA with in-person intake, but with different hours (9:00 am-3:00 pm Monday-Friday, 9:00 am-1:00 pm Saturday; 211OC last verified 2026-01-12) and English/Spanish service; the center's own page lists no Wednesday hours. 211OC also still lists Mary's Kitchen at this same address, while Mary's Kitchen's own site now describes a food rescue based in Anaheim."}, {"id": "ocie-sbdc", "name": "Orange County Inland Empire Small Business Development Center (OCIE SBDC)", "organization": "Orange County Inland Empire SBDC Network", "category": "microenterprise", "tags": ["small-business", "business-plan", "consulting", "access-to-capital", "no-cost", "startup", "training"], "description": "No-cost one-on-one consulting and training for people starting or growing a small business in Orange, Riverside and San Bernardino counties, including help writing a business plan and preparing a loan package for lenders.", "services": ["One-on-one business consulting", "SBDC Start: four-week no-cost startup series", "Business plan help", "Loan package preparation and introductions to lenders", "Cohort training programs (for example EATS for food businesses)"], "eligibility": null, "population": ["adults", "entrepreneurs"], "how_to_access": "appointment", "referral_required": false, "phone": "(800) 616-7232", "address": null, "city": null, "hours": null, "languages": null, "cost": "No cost", "website": "https://ociesmallbusiness.org/", "source_url": "https://ociesmallbusiness.org/", "source_quote": "We provide no-cost consulting to small businesses across Orange, Riverside, and San Bernardino counties.", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "high", "notes": "Advising, not money: it is not a lender, but its finance center helps prepare a loan package and connects clients with banks, CDFIs and nonprofit lenders. Starts with a 15-minute intake phone call. Not designed for people experiencing homelessness; ask what address, ID or business registration is needed."}, {"id": "accessity-small-business-loans", "name": "Accessity small business loans ($300 to $25,000 start-up and expansion loans)", "organization": "Accessity", "category": "microenterprise", "tags": ["microloan", "startup", "nonprofit-lender", "southern-california", "business-coaching"], "description": "Nonprofit lender serving Southern California entrepreneurs with limited access to traditional financing. Offers term loans from $300 to $25,000 for start-up or growing businesses (and larger loans up to $250,000), plus business support.", "services": ["Term loans $300 to $25,000 for start-up or growing businesses", "Loans $25,001 to $250,000", "Business coaching and peer support network"], "eligibility": "Must be current on all personal financial obligations; live/work in Southern California; use the proceeds of the loan for your business; be at least 18 years of age and demonstrate good character; business must be a legal entity.", "population": ["adults", "entrepreneurs"], "how_to_access": "online", "referral_required": false, "phone": "619.884.8467", "address": null, "city": null, "hours": null, "languages": null, "cost": "8.99% – 14.99% fixed, simple interest; no application fees; closing costs financed into the loan", "website": "https://accessity.org/", "source_url": "https://accessity.org/loans/", "source_quote": "From $300 to $25,000 term loans for startup or growing businesses", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "medium", "notes": "Medium confidence: the page footer shows 'Copyright 2024' and product text refers to 2023 financial statements, so terms may have changed. 619.884.8467 is the staff line the site lists for Orange County; the main office line is 619.795.7250 (San Diego). These are loans with a credit review, and the business must be a legal entity. Both are real barriers for many clients."}, {"id": "jfla-zero-interest-loans", "name": "Jewish Free Loan Association (JFLA) zero-interest loans", "organization": "Jewish Free Loan Association", "category": "microenterprise", "tags": ["interest-free-loan", "small-business-loan", "startup-loan", "personal-loan", "guarantor-required"], "description": "Nonprofit offering zero-interest, zero-fee loans to individuals, families, students and small businesses in Los Angeles, Ventura, Orange and Santa Barbara counties. Business loans are considered case by case up to $50,000; personal or emergency loans go up to $15,000 with two guarantors.", "services": ["Startup and small business loans (case by case, up to $50,000)", "Personal/emergency loans (up to $15,000)", "Education loans"], "eligibility": "All applicants must be over 18, have a permanent residence in Los Angeles, Ventura, Orange, or Santa Barbara County, have proof of income and a valid CA state ID. Personal loans require two qualified guarantors/co-signers.", "population": ["adults", "entrepreneurs", "students"], "how_to_access": "online", "referral_required": false, "phone": "310-735-4911", "address": null, "city": null, "hours": null, "languages": null, "cost": "Zero interest, zero fees", "website": "https://www.jfla.org/", "source_url": "https://www.jfla.org/", "source_quote": "JFLA is a non-profit offering zero-interest, zero-fee loans to individuals, families, students and small businesses in Los Angeles, Ventura, Orange, and Santa Barbara counties.", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "high", "notes": "Eligibility is a real barrier for someone without housing: permanent residence, proof of income, a valid CA ID and guarantors are required. Phone is from https://www.jfla.org/about-jfla/contact-us and business loan terms from https://www.jfla.org/business-loans. JFLA describes itself as a remote agency with a Los Angeles mailing address."}, {"id": "cdc-s