g/our-services/", "source_quote": "Chrysalis’ services are free and available to all. Our only program requirement is that an individual is willing and able to work.", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "high", "notes": "Chrysalis reports that 74% of its clients are unstably housed. The need for an active phone number or email is a practical barrier; pair it with the phone entry. General information line (213) 394-2390. Address, phone and hours also match the County's Central SPA pocket guide (dated 2025)."}, {"id": "working-wardrobes-rebuilding-careers", "name": "Working Wardrobes: Rebuilding Careers Program", "organization": "Working Wardrobes", "category": "employment", "tags": ["career-coaching", "resume", "interview-clothing", "workshops", "veterans", "justice-impacted", "no-cost"], "description": "No-cost career readiness services for anyone facing self-described barriers to employment: career navigation, coaching on resumes and interviews, trainings and workshops, and an interview outfit for enrolled clients.", "services": ["Career navigation and an individualized plan", "Career coaching (resume, interview)", "Soft and hard skills training, workshops and certification programs", "Interview outfit ('Success Suit') for enrolled clients with an upcoming interview"], "eligibility": "Anyone facing self-described barriers to gainful employment (unemployed, underemployed, Veterans, justice-impacted, seniors, survivors of domestic violence, etc.). Interview clothing is for clients who are enrolled, actively engaged and have an upcoming job interview.", "population": ["adults", "veterans", "seniors"], "how_to_access": "mixed", "referral_required": false, "phone": "714-210-2460", "address": "2000 E McFadden Ave, Santa Ana, CA 92705", "city": "Santa Ana", "hours": "Mon-Fri: 8AM – 5PM", "languages": null, "cost": "No cost", "website": "https://www.workingwardrobes.org/", "source_url": "https://www.workingwardrobes.org/our-services/", "source_quote": "We offer no-cost services to anyone facing self-described barriers to gainful employment.", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "medium", "notes": "Medium confidence on location only: the home page announces 'WE'RE MOVING!' and says the Career Success Center and Donation Center are coming together under one roof, so the McFadden Ave address (from the Contact page) may change. Confirm by phone. Sign-up is an online 'referral form' a person can fill in themselves; staff say they respond within 3 business days."}, {"id": "dmv-no-fee-and-reduced-fee-id", "name": "California DMV no-fee and reduced-fee ID cards", "organization": "California Department of Motor Vehicles", "category": "id-documents", "tags": ["california-id", "fee-waiver", "homeless", "reduced-fee", "dl-937", "senior"], "description": "The DMV may issue an ID card at no fee to a person who is homeless as defined by the McKinney-Vento Act, and at a reduced fee to people who meet income requirements for certain assistance programs. Applications are finished in person at a DMV office.", "services": ["No-fee ID card for people who are homeless", "Reduced-fee ID card (with a completed DL 937 from an assistance program)", "No-fee senior ID card (62 or older)"], "eligibility": "No fee: a \"homeless person\" as defined by the McKinney-Vento Act (includes a homeless child or youth, and an individual or family fleeing domestic violence or similar danger). Reduced fee: meet income requirements for selected governmental or non-profit assistance programs and bring a completed DL 937. Senior no-fee card: at least 62 years old.", "population": ["adults", "youth", "seniors"], "how_to_access": "mixed", "referral_required": null, "phone": null, "address": null, "city": null, "hours": null, "languages": null, "cost": "No fee or reduced fee if eligible", "website": "https://www.dmv.ca.gov/", "source_url": "https://www.dmv.ca.gov/portal/driver-licenses-identification-cards/identification-id-cards/", "source_quote": "You may be eligible for a no-fee ID card if you are a “homeless person” as defined by the McKinney-Vento Act.", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "high", "notes": "Statewide; use any DMV field office. The page names form DL 937 for the reduced fee but does not say, on this page, what proof of homelessness is needed for the no-fee card. Ask the DMV or a homeless services provider. Applicants still have to prove identity and, for a first California card, residency; that is often the real obstacle."}, {"id": "homeless-fee-exempt-birth-certificate", "name": "Free certified birth certificate for people experiencing homelessness (AB 1733 / AB 2490)", "organization": "California Department of Public Health: Vital Records, and county recorders (for Orange County births: Orange County Clerk-Recorder)", "category": "id-documents", "tags": ["birth-certificate", "fee-waiver", "affidavit", "vital-records", "homeless"], "description": "California law lets a person who is homeless get a certified copy of their birth record without a fee, from the county where they were born or from the State Registrar, using an Affidavit of Homeless Status signed by a homeless services provider.", "services": ["Fee-exempt certified copy of a birth record (one per application)"], "eligibility": "Meets the federal McKinney-Vento definition of homeless person or homeless child or youth, and can verify homeless status. The affidavit must be signed by both a homeless services provider and the person requesting the record.", "population": ["adults", "youth", "families"], "how_to_access": "mixed", "referral_required": true, "phone": "(714) 834-2500", "address": "601 N. Ross St., Santa Ana, CA 92701", "city": "Santa Ana", "hours": "8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Monday - Friday", "languages": null, "cost": "No fee with a completed affidavit; the Orange County Clerk-Recorder fee schedule otherwise lists a birth certificate at $34.00", "website": "https://www.ocrecorder.com/clerk-services/vital-records", "source_url": "https://www.cdph.ca.gov/Programs/CHSI/Pages/Assembly-Bill-(AB)-1733.aspx", "source_quote": "allows a homeless person, or a homeless child or youth, to be eligible to receive a copy of a birth record without a fee", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "medium", "notes": "Medium confidence: the State page and affidavit establish the right, but the Orange County Clerk-Recorder pages fetched (vital records page and fee schedule effective 2026-09-01) do not mention the fee exemption or how to present the affidavit, so call first. Phone, address and hours are the Clerk-Recorder's Central Office, for people born in Orange County; branches are at 222 S. Harbor Blvd, Ste. 110A, Anaheim and 24031 El Toro Rd., Ste. 150, Laguna Hills (9:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.). People born elsewhere apply to that county or the State. The affidavit lists who counts as a homeless services provider, including a nonprofit agency funded to serve homeless people. In-person applicants must fill in the application online first and bring valid government photo ID, which can be circular for someone with no ID."}, {"id": "oc-social-services-agency-benefits", "name": "County of Orange Social Services Agency: CalFresh, Medi-Cal, CalWORKs and General Relief", "organization": "County of Orange Social Services Agency (SSA)", "category": "benefits", "tags": ["calfresh", "medi-cal", "calworks", "general-relief", "capi", "benefitscal", "ebt"], "description": "County agency that takes applications for CalFresh food benefits, Medi-Cal, CalWORKs and General Relief. People can apply for CalFresh online at BenefitsCal.com, by phone, or in person at a regional center.", "services": ["CalFresh applications and EBT", "Medi-Cal applications", "CalWORKs", "General Relief", "Cash Assistance Program for Immigrants (CAPI)"], "eligibility": "CalFresh: must be a resident of Orange County and report all household members' income and property; limits vary with household size and ages. Other programs have their own rules.