s passes to meet eligibility and verification requirements", "Disability accommodations (home application, phone interview, mail-in application)"], "eligibility": "Applicants must verify their circumstances, including identification for all adults who apply, a Social Security card or other acceptable documentation, income, property, registration with the CalFresh Employment & Training / General Relief Work Program, and documentation of legal immigration status. The application includes a Repayment Agreement.", "population": ["adults"], "how_to_access": "mixed", "referral_required": false, "phone": "800-281-9799", "address": null, "city": null, "hours": "Call Center: Weekdays (Monday-Friday) from 7:30 a.m. to 5 p.m.", "languages": null, "cost": null, "website": "https://ssa.ocgov.com/cash-calfresh/general-relief", "source_url": "https://ssa.ocgov.com/cash-calfresh/how-apply/how-apply-general-relief", "source_quote": "You can apply for General Relief Benefits by phone (800-281-9799 / TTY 714-834-8500), in person at select Social Services Agency office locations, or by mail.", "verified_date": "2026-10-13", "confidence": "high", "notes": "Identification and a Social Security card are required verifications, so pair this with the ID-documents entries. People whose disability prevents an office visit can ask for a supervisor at the same number to arrange a home or phone application. In-person offices are listed in the Social Services Agency entry."}, {"id": "octa-reduced-fares", "name": "OC Bus reduced fares (seniors 60+, people with disabilities, college students, youth)", "organization": "Orange County Transportation Authority (OCTA)", "category": "transportation", "tags": ["bus", "reduced-fare", "senior", "disability", "youth-ride-free", "wave-card", "fare-capping"], "description": "Reduced OC Bus fares for riders 60 and older and people with disabilities ($0.75 single fare instead of the $2.00 regular fare), free rides for youth 18 and under, and college discounts. R